			"date": "2023-03-18T22:22:48.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> Love simple tab groups extension. Discard a group to unload the tabs from memory but still in the browser. Archive a group to completely unload the tabs from the browser (effectively bookmarked). Pop open the vertical sidebar to manage them all. I start a fresh group pretty much every day. Less stressful than having to close tabs, but more manageable than keeping them open. I can quite understand how you've got to 3k.</p>",
